ross W1–W3), logged in [journal.md](file:///workspace/agent/journal.md) and committed (`28a8c2e`).\n\nResidual analysis via [compare_runs.py](file:///workspace/research/compare_runs.py) and [study_iter2_weekend_dynamics.py](file:///workspace/research/study_iter2_weekend_dynamics.py) revealed that Monday–Thursday prompts are already within `0.2%–1.0%` of `field_median`, while the largest remaining gap sits on Friday/Saturday transitions due to:\n1. Evolution in weekend off-hours quoting volatility relative to spring/summer static curves (observable causally across the 4 weekends in `CONTEXT_DAYS = 30`).\n2. Trade-drought distortion of fast EWMAs during thin weekend hours.\n3. Closed-exchange weekend mean reversion (`VR(3h/5m) = 0.32–0.73` on `AAPLX`, `GOOGLX`, `SP500`, `SPCX`).\n\nFor **Iteration 2**, I implemented Online Empirical-Bayes 30-day session adaptation (`_online_session_adjustments`), information-weighted EWMAs (`_activity_ewma_terminals`), and closed-exchange weekend Ornstein-Uhlenbeck tethering (`_build_cum_log_returns`) in [modeling.py](file:///workspace/agent/modeling.py). The paired 54-cell, 1000-path evaluation is now running in the background.\nRunning [calibrate_iter3_stochvol_t.py](file:///workspace/research/calibrate_iter3_stochvol_t.py) across `\u003c= 2026-08-10` prompts to calibrate Student-$t$ degrees of freedom, intrapath AR(1) log-volatility, leverage correlation, and scale against `calculate_total_score_for_miner` (already showing `-0.62%` on `CRYPTO_1H` in early lines); waiting ~15s for all three competitions to finish.\nRefining the `\u003c= 2026-08-10` Student-$t$ + stationary AR(1) log-volatility parameter grid across 845 `CRYPTO_1H`, `CRYPTO_24H`, and `COM_EQU_24H` prompts; waiting ~15s for completion.\n**Iteration 2** (`iter2b` TradFi-gated weekend EB adaptation + activity-weighted EWMA + closed-exchange weekend OU tethering) improved **23 / 24** `COM_EQU_24H` cells (`-0.35%` W1, `-1.05%` W2, `-0.26%` W3; Friday ratio `1.084 -\u003e 